1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:02,660
Wealth, Fame, Power.

2
00:00:03,040 --> 00:00:04,597
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

3
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:07,237
attained this and everything
else the world had to offer,

4
00:00:07,320 --> 00:00:10,496
and his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

5
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:11,975
You want my treasure?

6
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:13,420
You can have it.

7
00:00:13,620 --> 00:00:16,620
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

8
00:00:16,860 --> 00:00:19,060
Now you just have to find it.

9
00:00:20,980 --> 00:00:24,237
These words lured men to
the Grand Line in pursuit

10
00:00:24,320 --> 00:00:26,397
of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine.

11
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:29,600
This is the time known
as the Great Pirate Era.

12
00:00:30,100 --> 00:00:35,240
Come aboard and bring along
all your hopes and dreams.

13
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:40,460
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for.

14
00:00:41,700 --> 00:00:42,680
One Piece.

15
00:00:48,040 --> 00:00:52,557
Compass left behind,
it'll only slow us down.

16
00:00:52,640 --> 00:00:58,477
Your heart will be your guide,
raise the sails and take the helm.

17
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:03,897
That legendary place that
the end of the map reveals.

18
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:10,117
Is only legendary till
someone proves it real?

19
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:14,437
Through it all, through
all the trouble of times!

20
00:01:14,520 --> 00:01:16,817
Through the heartache
and through the pain.

21
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:21,057
Know that I will be there to stand by you.

22
00:01:21,140 --> 00:01:24,300
Just like I know you'll stand by me.

23
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:30,580
So come aboard and bring along
All your hopes and dreams.

24
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:35,980
Together we will find everything
That we're looking for?

25
00:01:37,180 --> 00:01:39,697
There's always room for you!

26
00:01:39,780 --> 00:01:42,420
If you wanna be my friend.

27
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:46,780
We are, we are on a cruise!

28
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:49,720
We are

29
00:01:51,680 --> 00:01:52,820
Ah! Ah!

30
00:01:57,880 --> 00:02:06,540
Ahhhh!

31
00:02:10,820 --> 00:02:11,650
Huh?

32
00:02:11,733 --> 00:02:12,563
Ah!

33
00:02:13,140 --> 00:02:13,970
Ahhhhh!

34
00:02:14,960 --> 00:02:16,360
Aaaaah!

35
00:02:29,440 --> 00:02:30,577
Is his arm okay?

36
00:02:30,660 --> 00:02:34,197
If he took a single step back, his
arm would have been ripped off.

37
00:02:34,280 --> 00:02:37,057
Yeah, but he wasn't thinking
about how animal fangs work;

38
00:02:37,140 --> 00:02:39,552
that'd require a tiny bit of brain power.

39
00:02:40,980 --> 00:02:41,997
Is he okay?

40
00:02:42,080 --> 00:02:44,680
You think Big Bro
Luffy's arm will make it?

41
00:02:58,680 --> 00:03:00,280
Hey, where'd he go?

42
00:03:01,080 --> 00:03:02,600
Luffy, the sea!

43
00:03:05,740 --> 00:03:07,480
Hey, look, a shark!

44
00:03:08,680 --> 00:03:10,460
No, that's Arlong!

45
00:03:13,100 --> 00:03:15,140
So wait, you an under?

46
00:03:16,360 --> 00:03:17,190
Oh, crap.

47
00:03:17,480 --> 00:03:18,421
This isn't good.

48
00:03:18,520 --> 00:03:21,696
His abilities double in
strength when he's underwater.

49
00:03:24,360 --> 00:03:28,760
Once my momentum in the water builds
up, it's impossible to stop me.

50
00:03:29,060 --> 00:03:34,500
This is precisely the kind of ability that
makes us fishmen all the more superior.

51
00:03:36,020 --> 00:03:37,360
Did he run away?

52
00:03:44,200 --> 00:03:45,620
Ah, it's time.

53
00:03:46,360 --> 00:03:47,240
Soap!

54
00:03:55,020 --> 00:03:56,177
Oh no!

55
00:03:56,260 --> 00:03:57,600
A torpedo?

56
00:04:00,660 --> 00:04:03,260
Something just flew out of the sea!

57
00:04:12,060 --> 00:04:13,380
Wow!

58
00:04:14,400 --> 00:04:15,230
Wow.

59
00:04:15,313 --> 00:04:17,600
I'm impressed you could
dodge that. Good job.

60
00:04:17,980 --> 00:04:21,804
But the longer you evade your
death, the more painful it will be.

61
00:04:24,500 --> 00:04:25,840
Shark... DOGE!

62
00:04:39,380 --> 00:04:40,210
Whoa.

63
00:04:40,293 --> 00:04:42,780
Just what kind of bones
does that crazy shark have?

64
00:04:43,380 --> 00:04:45,380
His nose crushed the ground.

65
00:04:46,520 --> 00:04:47,350
Charge!

66
00:05:04,400 --> 00:05:06,100
Hey, Luffy, hide!

67
00:05:06,340 --> 00:05:08,164
Marlon went into the sea again!

68
00:05:10,920 --> 00:05:13,460
Hurry up, Big Bro, you
gotta hide from him.

69
00:05:13,680 --> 00:05:16,092
He's setting his sights on you right now.

70
00:05:19,740 --> 00:05:21,160
Get out of there!

71
00:05:25,520 --> 00:05:26,640
I won't hide.

72
00:05:27,620 --> 00:05:29,240
Stop being so stupid.

73
00:05:29,500 --> 00:05:32,800
Go run for cover before you
become a target. No way!

74
00:05:33,080 --> 00:05:34,497
I'm not running anywhere.

75
00:05:34,580 --> 00:05:36,874
I'm gonna catch him and break his nose.

76
00:05:38,820 --> 00:05:39,840
Ya shark!

77
00:05:43,280 --> 00:05:44,740
You got some nerve.

78
00:05:45,140 --> 00:05:48,980
Or you realize that it's
pointless to try and hide from me.

79
00:05:49,900 --> 00:05:53,157
Did you hear us telling you that
you should go somewhere and hide?

80
00:05:53,240 --> 00:05:55,077
You barely escaped his last attacks!

81
00:05:55,160 --> 00:05:57,817
If he lands just one
direct hit, it'll kill you!

82
00:05:57,900 --> 00:05:59,140
Luffy, listen to us!

83
00:05:59,240 --> 00:06:00,240
Go and hide!

84
00:06:01,340 --> 00:06:02,720
Now Gum-Gum!

85
00:06:05,920 --> 00:06:06,750
SHIELD!

86
00:06:08,280 --> 00:06:10,260
Hey wait, what's that position?

87
00:06:10,480 --> 00:06:12,715
I don't think that'll stop the attack.

88
00:06:12,920 --> 00:06:15,557
I'll get double the
speed from this distance.

89
00:06:15,640 --> 00:06:18,228
This time I'll pierce
your heart, Weber Man.

90
00:06:18,600 --> 00:06:20,300
Now, take this!

91
00:06:22,380 --> 00:06:23,210
SHOTTERS!

92
00:06:29,140 --> 00:06:30,260
He's here!

93
00:06:43,380 --> 00:06:44,400
Oh no!

94
00:06:44,720 --> 00:06:46,680
Did he get hit? He's fine.

95
00:06:46,940 --> 00:06:48,764
He somehow managed to avoid it.

96
00:06:51,020 --> 00:06:52,060
It's over!

97
00:06:52,340 --> 00:06:54,120
That attack won't work now!

98
00:06:54,920 --> 00:06:55,900
Sure, die!

99
00:07:03,020 --> 00:07:04,440
You bastard!

100
00:07:04,800 --> 00:07:06,260
I was just pure luck!

101
00:07:08,360 --> 00:07:09,400
That's it!

102
00:07:10,100 --> 00:07:11,460
Gum-Gum!

103
00:07:11,980 --> 00:07:13,240
Paper nine!

104
00:07:44,620 --> 00:07:46,040
Is he dead?

105
00:07:48,060 --> 00:07:50,660
Do you see the intensity in his eyes?

106
00:07:50,840 --> 00:07:54,940
Oh no, it's the same expression that
sea kings make before they snap!

107
00:07:55,760 --> 00:07:58,520
He must have snapped
with Luffy's last attack?

108
00:08:00,880 --> 00:08:01,900
His eyes!

109
00:08:02,080 --> 00:08:03,904
I've never seen them like that.

110
00:08:04,320 --> 00:08:06,100
You wretched human!

111
00:08:09,040 --> 00:08:10,900
What have you done to me?

112
00:08:11,360 --> 00:08:12,880
A mighty fish man!

113
00:08:24,100 --> 00:08:25,037
Whoa, that was crazy.

114
00:08:25,120 --> 00:08:29,002
It didn't actually hurt, but I can
tell he's really, like, madder.

115
00:08:39,540 --> 00:08:41,300
Oh man, what was that?

116
00:08:41,540 --> 00:08:42,640
The saw blade!

117
00:08:43,060 --> 00:08:44,820
That thing is gigantic!

118
00:08:55,720 --> 00:08:56,550
Aaaaaah!

119
00:08:58,860 --> 00:08:59,690
Aaaaaah!

120
00:09:02,180 --> 00:09:03,320
Aaaaaah! Aaaaaah!

121
00:09:05,280 --> 00:09:06,110
Aaaaaah!

122
00:09:07,100 --> 00:09:07,930
Aaaaaah!

123
00:09:08,013 --> 00:09:09,540
Micro Luffy! Micro Luffy!

124
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:11,600
He won't stop!

125
00:09:11,800 --> 00:09:13,212
Luffy will get cornered!

126
00:09:15,500 --> 00:09:18,880
Aaaaaah! Aaaaaah! Aaaaaah! Aaaaaah!

127
00:09:20,800 --> 00:09:22,620
He jumped in the building!

128
00:09:29,400 --> 00:09:32,420
the left window on the top floor.

129
00:09:34,220 --> 00:09:35,680
that's the room that.

130
00:09:37,360 --> 00:09:39,257
there's nowhere else to run.

131
00:09:39,340 --> 00:09:43,677
you and me here in the highest
level of our long park.

132
00:09:43,760 --> 00:09:45,617
what is this room?

133
00:09:45,700 --> 00:09:47,477
a lot of paper.

134
00:09:47,560 --> 00:09:49,817
this isn't just any room.

135
00:09:49,900 --> 00:09:54,380
This is the room where I make Nami
draw all of her C-charts for me.

136
00:09:55,040 --> 00:09:56,260
The nap room!

137
00:09:57,760 --> 00:09:59,360
This is Nami's room?

138
00:09:59,540 --> 00:10:03,140
These C-charts are what she's
worked on all these years.

139
00:10:04,980 --> 00:10:07,437
There is no one else on
the face of the planet that

140
00:10:07,520 --> 00:10:10,579
can draw C-charts with such
accuracy and efficiency.

141
00:10:11,800 --> 00:10:14,300
That young lady has a gift.

142
00:10:20,620 --> 00:10:26,260
And there really isn't anything as ultimately
regrettable as wasting natural talent.

143
00:10:26,540 --> 00:10:29,317
Staying here and drawing
up C-Charts for me is

144
00:10:29,400 --> 00:10:32,337
her only chance at living
up to her full potential.

145
00:10:32,420 --> 00:10:35,500
This pen is stained with blood.

146
00:10:36,180 --> 00:10:41,260
In order for me to attain world supremacy,
her C-Charts are absolutely vital.

147
00:10:43,800 --> 00:10:47,397
She will continue drawing her
C-Charts for my own ambitions.

148
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:51,957
And once her charts give me full
knowledge of all the world's oceans.

149
00:10:52,040 --> 00:10:55,557
We fishmen will be totally invincible!

150
00:10:55,640 --> 00:10:59,137
And the world shall kneel before us.

151
00:10:59,220 --> 00:11:02,177
The first step is this island.

152
00:11:02,260 --> 00:11:04,731
Then we'll move on to the whole East Blue.

153
00:11:07,120 --> 00:11:09,597
You could never use her like me?

154
00:11:09,680 --> 00:11:12,140
She would be wasted on you.

155
00:11:21,440 --> 00:11:22,270
What the?

156
00:11:22,680 --> 00:11:23,620
The shark cell.

157
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:25,420
It won't budge.

158
00:11:29,140 --> 00:11:29,970
Now!

159
00:11:32,020 --> 00:11:33,000
Use her!

160
00:11:35,020 --> 00:11:36,020
What's happening?

161
00:11:36,360 --> 00:11:37,772
Are they still fighting?

162
00:11:38,500 --> 00:11:40,000
What's going on up there?

163
00:11:40,200 --> 00:11:42,376
Damn it, big bro Luffy, are you okay?

164
00:11:42,640 --> 00:11:45,111
I wish we knew what was going on up there.

165
00:11:49,680 --> 00:11:51,800
Luffy, you bastard.

166
00:11:52,260 --> 00:11:53,731
What do you take her for?

167
00:11:55,920 --> 00:12:00,060
She's an inferior creature, but
she has risen far above her peers.

168
00:12:00,360 --> 00:12:04,478
If all other humans are sewer rats,
then she's a feisty little kitten.

169
00:12:05,040 --> 00:12:06,628
After all, she is adorable.

170
00:12:07,120 --> 00:12:10,220
She has her place, and
it's here beside me.

171
00:12:10,720 --> 00:12:12,249
Can't you understand that?

172
00:12:12,560 --> 00:12:15,437
I can give her everything she needs.

173
00:12:15,520 --> 00:12:20,900
And the only thing she has to do is continue
drawing those marvelous charts for me.

174
00:12:22,560 --> 00:12:27,060
So Nami will forever be my tool or no?

175
00:12:28,040 --> 00:12:29,840
She'll be my friend.

176
00:12:38,480 --> 00:12:39,600
What is that?

177
00:12:42,060 --> 00:12:43,017
A desk.

178
00:12:43,100 --> 00:12:45,337
It's a desk.

179
00:12:45,420 --> 00:12:47,957
It's okay.

180
00:12:48,040 --> 00:12:50,897
It was just a desk. Man. I was scared.

181
00:12:50,980 --> 00:12:52,057
I thought that was big.

182
00:12:52,140 --> 00:12:52,970
Bro.

183
00:12:53,053 --> 00:12:53,883
Luffy.

184
00:12:53,966 --> 00:12:54,796
For sure.

185
00:12:54,879 --> 00:12:55,709
Hold on.

186
00:12:55,792 --> 00:12:56,797
I don't want to hear that
kind of talk from you.

187
00:12:56,880 --> 00:12:58,837
Have you lost your faith? What?

188
00:12:58,920 --> 00:12:59,750
No.

189
00:12:59,833 --> 00:13:01,637
You were scared too. Johnny.

190
00:13:01,720 --> 00:13:02,577
Don't be stupid.

191
00:13:02,660 --> 00:13:04,277
I just uh well you know.

192
00:13:04,360 --> 00:13:05,557
I thought it was Arlong.

193
00:13:05,640 --> 00:13:06,537
Flying through the air.

194
00:13:06,620 --> 00:13:08,137
What a load of crap.

195
00:13:08,220 --> 00:13:10,497
You were scared. Admit. Admit.

196
00:13:10,580 --> 00:13:12,197
What you jerk. Admit that.

197
00:13:12,280 --> 00:13:13,477
I know Arlong's going down.

198
00:13:13,560 --> 00:13:17,207
There's no way that big bro Luffy
is going to lose this fight.

199
00:13:22,680 --> 00:13:23,510
Whoa.

200
00:13:23,593 --> 00:13:24,423
What's going on?

201
00:13:24,506 --> 00:13:27,084
Why is all that stuff
being thrown out of there?

202
00:13:38,060 --> 00:13:40,880
Alright, as of today,
this will be your room,

203
00:13:41,280 --> 00:13:45,100
your desk, your pens, everything
you'll need is in here.

204
00:13:48,200 --> 00:13:49,600
Stop it now!

205
00:13:52,240 --> 00:13:53,070
The charts!

206
00:13:55,040 --> 00:13:55,870
My charts!

207
00:13:59,440 --> 00:14:02,340
Dumb rat, you can't trick me that easily.

208
00:14:03,100 --> 00:14:05,220
Trying to draw up fake charts.

209
00:14:07,380 --> 00:14:09,257
I can't believe you waste your time!

210
00:14:09,340 --> 00:14:11,281
Drawing crap like this in secret.

211
00:14:14,440 --> 00:14:16,857
If you ever try to pull
a stunt like this again?

212
00:14:16,940 --> 00:14:19,037
I'll drag all those villagers in here!

213
00:14:19,120 --> 00:14:21,757
And make you watch as I
crush every single one!

214
00:14:21,840 --> 00:14:23,380
Just like with her.

215
00:14:29,700 --> 00:14:30,657
Damn you!

216
00:14:30,740 --> 00:14:34,916
That's eight years worth of work,
eight years of planning and ambition!

217
00:14:40,540 --> 00:14:42,860
Fell in here, don't you know?

218
00:14:49,280 --> 00:14:52,060
Wow, this fight is so freaking intense.

219
00:14:53,120 --> 00:14:55,500
Yeah, a fight to the death, definitely.

220
00:15:04,360 --> 00:15:05,680
Thank you.

221
00:15:11,920 --> 00:15:14,080
Now you've got too far!

222
00:15:16,560 --> 00:15:21,020
You keep jabbering on about
how much better fish men are,

223
00:15:21,180 --> 00:15:23,480
and how much you need those sea charts.

224
00:15:23,780 --> 00:15:26,857
I don't understand
anything about that stuff.

225
00:15:26,940 --> 00:15:31,020
I've finally figured out how to save her!

226
00:15:36,240 --> 00:15:39,100
This room isn't anything
but our jail cell.

227
00:15:39,420 --> 00:15:41,820
There's only one way for Nami to escape.

228
00:15:42,140 --> 00:15:44,260
I've got to tear this place apart.

229
00:15:45,840 --> 00:15:46,670
Conker!

230
00:15:47,600 --> 00:15:48,700
You fool.

231
00:15:49,300 --> 00:15:52,800
Arlong Park cannot be brought
down by some inferior human,

232
00:15:52,980 --> 00:15:55,417
especially not by some
rubbery freak like you!

233
00:15:55,500 --> 00:15:58,260
Start to drown!

234
00:15:59,100 --> 00:16:02,340
Oh, shit!

235
00:16:45,700 --> 00:16:46,660
Oh no!

236
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:49,412
It looks like Arlong Park is coming down!

237
00:16:50,120 --> 00:16:51,580
It's gonna collapse!

238
00:16:51,860 --> 00:16:53,320
Everybody run for cover!

239
00:16:54,740 --> 00:16:56,640
Make sense! We gotta go!

240
00:16:56,740 --> 00:16:57,737
Luffy's still inside!

241
00:16:57,820 --> 00:16:59,080
Make sense! We can't!

242
00:16:59,200 --> 00:17:00,435
Luffy's still inside!

243
00:17:05,920 --> 00:17:06,750
Luffy!

244
00:17:21,080 --> 00:17:21,910
Luffy...

245
00:17:30,360 --> 00:17:32,120
It's... Luffy.

246
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:50,600
What the hell?

247
00:17:50,860 --> 00:17:52,140
What's that noise?

248
00:17:57,160 --> 00:17:58,120
Roofing.

249
00:18:12,080 --> 00:18:15,200
Warlong Park has fallen.

250
00:18:15,840 --> 00:18:16,700
Big bro.

251
00:18:17,160 --> 00:18:20,097
I just wonder what went on in there.

252
00:18:20,180 --> 00:18:22,897
We gotta know who won?

253
00:18:22,980 --> 00:18:24,377
With all that debris!

254
00:18:24,460 --> 00:18:26,280
Looks like?

255
00:18:27,920 --> 00:18:28,800
Luffy?

256
00:18:39,640 --> 00:18:41,020
It's Luffy!

257
00:18:42,100 --> 00:18:43,440
Big bro? No!

258
00:18:48,720 --> 00:18:51,200
He's just standing there. What's wrong?

259
00:18:58,480 --> 00:18:59,310
NAMI!

260
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:06,830
NAMI!

261
00:19:06,913 --> 00:19:08,077
YOU 'LL ALWAYS BE MY

262
00:19:08,160 --> 00:19:12,748
Fire

263
00:19:20,780 --> 00:19:22,180
Yeah.

264
00:19:43,340 --> 00:19:45,437
Now I'm done, I'll keep you near.

265
00:19:45,520 --> 00:19:50,120
As I drift away, I pray you'll
watch me as I disappear!

266
00:19:55,520 --> 00:20:00,117
As I watch the sunrise, I begin to wonder?

267
00:20:00,200 --> 00:20:04,860
What could be the reason
it's so hot inside?

268
00:20:05,360 --> 00:20:10,917
No answer has come, but I can't
get away from what's true.

269
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:13,460
It's because of you!

270
00:20:16,360 --> 00:20:19,037
Show me how to catch those feelings.

271
00:20:19,120 --> 00:20:21,077
Get them to come back to me!

272
00:20:21,160 --> 00:20:23,397
I'll do what I must be.

273
00:20:23,480 --> 00:20:26,137
Cause they're everything I want to be!

274
00:20:26,220 --> 00:20:28,657
Wrap these arms around my dreams.

275
00:20:28,740 --> 00:20:30,737
And pull them back from yesterday.

276
00:20:30,820 --> 00:20:36,120
If I'm holding hands for you,
I'm sure that we can make a way?
